msgid "Simplified queries"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Normally, HQL queries are of this form: `from EntityName [where ...] [order "
"by ...]`, with optional elements\n"
"at the end."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If your select query does not start with `from`, `select` or `with`, we "
"support the following additional forms:"
msgstr ""

msgid "`order by ...` which will expand to `from EntityName order by ...`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`<singleAttribute>` (and single parameter) which will expand to `from "
"EntityName where <singleAttribute> = ?`"
msgstr ""

msgid "`where <query>` will expand to `from EntityName where <query>`"
msgstr ""

msgid "`<query>` will expand to `from EntityName where <query>`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If your update query does not start with `update`, we support the following "
"additional forms:"
msgstr ""

msgid "`from EntityName ...` which will expand to `update EntityName ...`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`set? <singleAttribute>` (and single parameter) which will expand to `update "
"EntityName set <singleAttribute> = ?`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`set? <update-query>` will expand to `update EntityName set <update-query>`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If your delete query does not start with `delete`, we support the following "
"additional forms:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`from EntityName ...` which will expand to `delete from EntityName ...`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`<singleAttribute>` (and single parameter) which will expand to `delete from "
"EntityName where <singleAttribute> = ?`"
msgstr ""

msgid "`<query>` will expand to `delete from EntityName where <query>`"
msgstr ""

