msgid "Query projection"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Query projection can be done with the `project(Class)` method on the "
"`PanacheQuery` object that is returned by the `find()` methods."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can use it to restrict which fields will be returned by the database."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Hibernate will use **DTO projection** and generate a SELECT clause with the "
"attributes from the projection class.\n"
"This is also called **dynamic instantiation** or **constructor expression**, "
"more info can be found on the Hibernate guide:\n"
"link:{hibernate-orm-docs-url}#hql-select-clause[hql select clause]"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The projection class needs to have a constructor that contains all its "
"attributes, this constructor will be used to\n"
"instantiate the projection DTO instead of using the entity class. This class "
"must have a matching constructor with all the class attributes as parameters."
""
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `@RegisterForReflection` annotation instructs Quarkus to keep the class "
"and its members during the native compilation. More details about the "
"`@RegisterForReflection` annotation can be found on  the xref:writing-native-"
"applications-tips.adoc#registerForReflection[native application tips] page."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We use public fields here, but you can use private fields and getters/"
"setters if you prefer."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This constructor will be used by Hibernate, it must be the only constructor "
"in your class and have all the class attributes as parameters."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The implementation of the `project(Class)` method uses the constructor's "
"parameter names to build the select clause of the query,\n"
"so the compiler must be configured to store parameter names inside the "
"compiled class.\n"
"This is enabled by default if you are using the Quarkus Maven archetype. If "
"you are not using it, add the property `<maven.compiler.parameters>true</"
"maven.compiler.parameters>` to your `pom.xml`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If in the DTO projection object you have a field from a referenced entity, "
"you can use the `@ProjectedFieldName` annotation to provide the path for the "
"SELECT statement."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `ownerName` DTO constructor's parameter will be loaded from the `owner."
"name` HQL property."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `@ProjectedFieldName` annotation also supports HQL expressions, "
"including aggregate functions.\n"
"This is particularly useful for GROUP BY queries:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In case you want to project an entity in a class with nested classes, you "
"can use the `@NestedProjectedClass` annotation on those nested classes."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This annotation can be used when you want to project `@Embedded` entity or "
"`@ManyToOne`, `@OneToOne` relation.\n"
"It does not support `@OneToMany` or `@ManyToMany` relation."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"It is also possible to specify a HQL query with a select clause. In this "
"case, the projection class must have a constructor\n"
"matching the values returned by the select clause:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Hibernate ORM will use this constructor. When the query has a select clause, "
"it is possible to have multiple constructors."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"It is not possible to have a HQL `select new` query and `.project(Class)` at "
"the same time - you need to pick one approach."
msgstr ""

msgid "For example, this will fail:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you need to have multiple constructors in your DTO, you must annotate the "
"constructor intended to generate a SELECT clause with @ProjectedConstructor:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This will use your annotated constructor to create the query. (`select new "
"PersonName(name) from ...`)"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If a DTO used in a projection has multiple constructors and is not properly "
"annotated, it may lead to *unexpected behavior*."
msgstr ""

msgid "The constructor resolution process follows this order:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Look for a constructor annotated with `@ProjectedConstructor`\n"
"This is the most explicit and preferred way to indicate which constructor "
"should be used."
msgstr ""

msgid "Look for parameters annotated with `@ProjectedFieldName`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Use the first non-parameterless constructor\n"
"If no annotations are found."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Fallback to the first constructor it finds, this could lead to multiple "
"problems or inconsistencies."
msgstr ""

